    <DataNode elementId="CPD-14762" textLabel="2&apos;&apos;-O-acetyl-ADP-ribose" type="Metabolite">
      <Xref identifier="BFNOPXRXIQJDHO-YDKGJHSESA-L" dataSource="InChIKey" />
      <Graphics centerX="546.1493530273438" centerY="765.4251098632812" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="3955e7" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="3955e7" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="AU4FS-3, SRI, keseler">&lt;i&gt;O&lt;/i&gt;-acetyl-ADP-ribose (OAADPr) is produced in protein deacetylation reactions catalyzed by NAD-dependent protein deacetylases such as |FRAME: EC-2.3.1.286| (also known as sirtuins) |CITS: [11106374][11893743]|, which regulate gene silencing, metabolic enzymes, and life span |CITS: [18940661][19041753][19410538][20203611]|. OAADPr has been implicated as a signaling molecule that modulates cellular processes and harnesses the regulation of metabolism and gene activity |CITS: [15999106][19251690][20176146]| It is accepted that the enzymatic product of sirtuins is |FRAME: CPD-14762|. However, |FRAME: CPD-14762| and |FRAME: CPD-14763| exist in equilibrium (48:52) in solution |CITS: [11893743]|.</Comment>
